### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS Lex V2 Models Bot named `example_lex_bot`. It also creates an IAM role named `lex_bot_role` that the Lex bot will use. The IAM role is configured to allow the Lex service to assume the role.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "lex_bot_role" {
  name = "lex_bot_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Sid    = ""
        Principal = {
          Service = "lexv2.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })

  tags = {
    created_by = "terraform"
  }
}

resource "aws_lexv2models_bot" "example_lex_bot" {
  name                    = "example_lex_bot"
  description             = "Example Lex Bot"
  idle_session_ttl_in_seconds = 300
  role_arn                = aws_iam_role.lex_bot_role.arn
  type                    = "Bot"

  data_privacy {
    child_directed = false
  }

  tags = {
    environment = "development"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-east-1` region.
2. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `lex_bot_role` is created. The role has an assume role policy that allows the Lex service (`lexv2.amazonaws.com`) to assume the role.
3. **AWS Lex V2 Models Bot**: A Lex bot named `example_lex_bot` is created. The bot is associated with the IAM role created earlier. The bot has a description, an idle session TTL of 300 seconds, and is of type `Bot`. The `data_privacy` block specifies that the bot is not child-directed. Tags are added for identification purposes.

