### Description
This Terraform configuration creates an IAM role named 'eks-cluster-1' with an assume role policy allowing the 'eks.amazonaws.com' service to assume the role. It attaches the 'AmazonEKSClusterPolicy' IAM policy to this role. Additionally, it defines an AWS EKS cluster named based on the provided cluster name variable and version, associating it with the IAM role. The cluster's VPC is configured with specified subnet IDs for networking, including private and public subnets in the specified AWS region.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "cluster_name" {
  description = "Name of the EKS cluster"
  default     = "my-eks-cluster"
}

variable "cluster_version" {
  description = "Version of the EKS cluster"
  default     = "1.24"
}

variable "vpc_id" {
  description = "ID of the VPC where the EKS cluster will be deployed"
  default     = "vpc-12345678"  # Replace with your VPC ID
}

variable "private_subnet_ids" {
  description = "List of private subnet IDs for the EKS cluster"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = ["subnet-12345678", "subnet-87654321"]  # Replace with your private subnet IDs
}

variable "public_subnet_ids" {
  description = "List of public subnet IDs for the EKS cluster"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = ["subnet-abcdef12", "subnet-34567890"]  # Replace with your public subnet IDs
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "eks_cluster_1" {
  name = "eks-cluster-1"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "eks.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "eks_cluster_1_amazon_eks_cluster_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonEKSClusterPolicy"
  role       = aws_iam_role.eks_cluster_1.name
}

resource "aws_eks_cluster" "eks_cluster" {
  name     = var.cluster_name
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.eks_cluster_1.arn
  version  = var.cluster_version

  vpc_config {
    subnet_ids = concat(var.private_subnet_ids, var.public_subnet_ids)
  }

  depends_on = [
    aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.eks_cluster_1_amazon_eks_cluster_policy,
  ]
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a default region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to your preferred region.
2. **Variables**: 
   - `cluster_name`: The name of the EKS cluster.
   - `cluster_version`: The version of the EKS cluster.
   - `vpc_id`: The ID of the VPC where the EKS cluster will be deployed.
   - `private_subnet_ids`: A list of private subnet IDs for the EKS cluster.
   - `public_subnet_ids`: A list of public subnet IDs for the EKS cluster.
3. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named 'eks-cluster-1' is created with an assume role policy allowing the 'eks.amazonaws.com' service to assume the role.
4. **IAM Role Policy Attachment**: The 'AmazonEKSClusterPolicy' IAM policy is attached to the IAM role.
5. **EKS Cluster**: An EKS cluster is defined with the specified name, version, and associated with the IAM role. The VPC configuration includes both private and public subnet IDs.

Make sure to replace the placeholder values for `vpc_id`, `private_subnet_ids`, and `public_subnet_ids` with actual values from your AWS environment.

