The Terraform program below sets up an AWS Lambda function triggered by a DynamoDB table. It includes creating an IAM role with the necessary permissions, defining the Lambda function, setting up the DynamoDB table with streaming enabled, and creating an event source mapping to connect the DynamoDB stream to the Lambda function. The configuration ensures that all required attributes are specified and that there are no undeclared resources or variables.

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Create an IAM role for the Lambda function
resource "aws_iam_role" "lambda_role" {
  name = "lambda_dynamodb_role"

