### Description
This Terraform configuration creates a DAX (DynamoDB Accelerator) cluster with the specified node type (`dax.r4.large`) and replication factor (`1`). It also sets up the necessary IAM role, subnet group, and parameter group required by the DAX cluster.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

# Create an IAM role for the DAX cluster
resource "aws_iam_role" "dax_iam_role" {
  name = "dax-cluster-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "dax.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Create a DAX subnet group
resource "aws_dax_subnet_group" "dax_subnet_group" {
  name       = "dax-subnet-group"
  subnet_ids = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0fedcba9876543210"]  # Replace with your subnet IDs
}

# Create a DAX parameter group
resource "aws_dax_parameter_group" "dax_parameter_group" {
  name = "dax-parameter-group"

  parameters {
    name  = "query-ttl-millis"
    value = "100000"
  }

  parameters {
    name  = "record-ttl-millis"
    value = "100000"
  }
}

# Create the DAX cluster
resource "aws_dax_cluster" "dax_cluster" {
  cluster_name       = "my-dax-cluster"
  iam_role_arn       = aws_iam_role.dax_iam_role.arn
  node_type          = "dax.r4.large"
  replication_factor = 1
  subnet_group_name  = aws_dax_subnet_group.dax_subnet_group.name
  parameter_group_name = aws_dax_parameter_group.dax_parameter_group.name
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a specific region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to your preferred region.
2. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `dax-cluster-role` is created with a trust policy allowing DAX to assume the role.
3. **DAX Subnet Group**: A subnet group named `dax-subnet-group` is created with a list of subnet IDs. Replace the placeholder subnet IDs with your actual subnet IDs.
4. **DAX Parameter Group**: A parameter group named `dax-parameter-group` is created with some default parameters.
5. **DAX Cluster**: The DAX cluster is created with the specified node type (`dax.r4.large`), replication factor (`1`), and references to the IAM role, subnet group, and parameter group.

Make sure to replace the placeholder subnet IDs with actual subnet IDs from your AWS account.

