The Terraform program defines the infrastructure for a video streaming site that distributes video content globally. It includes an AWS S3 bucket to store the video content, an AWS CloudFront distribution to serve the content via a CDN, an AWS Route53 zone for DNS management, and an AWS Route53 record to map a domain to the CloudFront distribution. The program also includes an AWS CloudFront origin access control to restrict access to the S3 bucket from CloudFront. Additionally, it ensures that the S3 bucket policy allows CloudFront to access the bucket.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "video_content_bucket" {
  bucket = "video-content-bucket-${random_string.suffix.result}"
  acl    = "private"

  tags = {
    Name = "Video Content Bucket"
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_policy" "video_content_bucket_policy" {
