### Description
This Terraform program creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and an associated target group. The ALB is configured to distribute incoming traffic to the target group, which in turn routes traffic to the specified targets. The configuration includes basic settings for the load balancer and target group, such as the VPC ID, port, protocol, and health checks.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "my_load_balancer" {
  name               = "my-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  security_groups    = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]
  subnets            = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0123456789abcdef1"]

  enable_deletion_protection = false

  tags = {
    Name = "MyALB"
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_target_group" "my_target_group" {
  name     = "my-target-group"
  port     = 80
  protocol = "HTTP"
  vpc_id   = "vpc-0123456789abcdef0"

  health_check {
    path                = "/"
    interval            = 30
    timeout             = 5
    healthy_threshold   = 5
    unhealthy_threshold = 2
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "MyTargetGroup"
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "my_listener" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.my_load_balancer.arn
  port              = "80"
  protocol          = "HTTP"

  default_action {
    type             = "forward"
    target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.my_target_group.arn
  }
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
- **Load Balancer (`aws_lb`)**: An Application Load Balancer is created with the name `my-alb`. It is configured to be internet-facing (`internal = false`) and uses the specified security groups and subnets.
- **Target Group (`aws_lb_target_group`)**: A target group named `my-target-group` is created, listening on port 80 with the HTTP protocol. It is associated with the specified VPC and includes a basic health check configuration.
- **Listener (`aws_lb_listener`)**: A listener is added to the load balancer to forward traffic on port 80 to the target group.

This configuration ensures that the load balancer and target group are properly set up and interconnected.

